mentOfReverseMortgages" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" scale="6" id="f-1066">1,115.4</ix:nonFraction> million repayments of reverse mortgage loans for the six months ended June 30, 2026 include $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="usd" contextRef="c-1" decimals="-5" name="onit:LoansHeldForSaleReverseMortgagesRepaymentsOfLoansPreviouslyHeldForInvestment" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" scale="6" id="f-1067">1,113.3</ix:nonFraction> million of repayments of loans that were classified as held for sale and previously held for investment, which remain presented as investing cash flows in the consolidated statement of cash flows.</span></div><div style="margin-top:6pt;text-indent:18pt"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">The following table presents the Fair value gains (losses) on reverse loans and HMBS-related borrowings included in earnings:</span></div><div style="margin-bottom:6pt;margin-top:3pt"><table style="border-collapse:collapse;display:inline-table;margin-bottom:5pt;vertical-align:text-bottom;width:100.000%"><tr><td style="width:1.0%"/><td style="width:42.759%"/><td style="width:0.1%"/><td style="width:1.0%"/><td style="width:12.496%"/><td style="width:0.1%"/><td style="width:0.1%"/><td style="width:0.384%"/><td style="width:0.1%"/><td style="width:1.0%"/><td style="width:12.496%"/><td style="width:0.1%"/><td style="width:0.1%"/><td style="width:0.384%"/><td style="width:0.1%"/><td style="width:1.0%"/><td style="width:12.496%"/><td style="width:0.1%"/><td style="width:0.1%"/><td style="width:0.384%"/><td style="width:0.1%"/><td style="width:1.0%"/><td style="width:12.501%"/><td style="width:0.1%"/></tr><tr><td colspan="3" style="padding:1.5pt 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"><div style="padding-left:9pt;text-indent:-9pt"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:100%">Fair value gains (losses) included in earnings</span></div></